	(text "CURRENT SENSE NOTES (per axis)\n- Shunt: 10 mOhm 4-terminal Kelvin (WSK2512, 1 W), high side after output filter\n- Amp: INA240A1, gain 20 V/V -> 0.2 V/A (200 mV/A)\n- REF1 = 3.3 V, REF2 = GND -> Vout = 1.65 V at 0 A (bidirectional)\n- Vout = 1.65 V + 0.2 V/A x I_coil   (+I = current from Icoil1 -> Icoil2)\n\nMEASUREMENT RANGE\n- Full scale: +/-1.65 V / 0.2 V/A = +/-8.25 A (ideal)\n- Usable: approx. +/-8.0 A (INA240 output swing limits near rails)\n- Shunt loss at 8 A: I^2 x R = 0.64 W (rated 1 W)\n\n12-BIT ADC RESOLUTION (VREF+ = VDDA = 3.3 V)\n- 1 LSB = 3.3 V / 4096 = 0.806 mV -> 0.806 mV / 0.2 V/A = approx. 4.0 mA per count\n- 0 A = code 2048,  I_coil [A] = (code - 2048) x 4.03 mA\n- Ratiometric: REF1 and VDDA share 3.3 V, so the 0 A point tracks supply drift\n- ADC pins: X = PA0 (ADC1_IN1), Y = PA4 (ADC2_IN17), Z = PB0 (ADC3_IN12)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.558 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6b1f0c52-3d8e-4a77-9e21-5c0a7f4e2b91")
	)
